IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Business Federation Act 2001 (Singapore) -- which companies become members of the Federation by force of law (s 5), the
-- subscription they must pay and its statutory cap (s 12), the information powers of the Board of Trustees and the offences that
-- back them (s 9), the make-up of the Council (s 4 and the Schedule), the matters needing the Board's approval (s 7(2)), who may
-- audit the accounts (s 8(2), (3)), dissolution (s 10) and the Act prevailing over the Federation's Constitution (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SBFA2001.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only
-- amendment annotated in the body is [33/2018], against s 12(4). The deposit's meta file records retrieval on 2026-10-01 as the
-- "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0207 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. For a business the answer is s 5 (am I a member without having joined?) and s 12 (what can I be made to
-- pay?). The Act is short (13 sections and a Schedule) and this row covers nearly all of it.
--
-- Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 2 except the definitions used here, s 3 (objects, stated but not decided on), s 6 (the
-- Minister's appointment and removal of trustees -- pure discretion), s 7(1) (the Board's general responsibilities), s 8(1), (4),
-- (5) (the Council's book-keeping duties and the regulation power), s 13 (regulations). No order under s 4(2) or s 5(2), and no
-- regulation, subscription schedule or Constitution of the Federation, was retrieved: the encoding assumes the threshold and
-- Schedule as printed.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Business Federation Act 2001 -- membership`

§§ `2 and 5 -- who becomes a member by force of law`

-- s 2: "local company" means "a company incorporated under Division 1 of Part 3 of the Companies Act 1967"; "foreign company" means
-- "a foreign company which is registered under Division 2 of Part 11 of the Companies Act 1967".
-- s 5(1): every (a) "local company which has a PAID-UP share capital of or above the amount of $500,000"; and (b) "foreign company
-- which has an AUTHORISED share capital of or above the amount of $500,000", "becomes, by virtue of this section and without
-- election, admission or appointment, a member of the Federation, unless the membership ... is terminated in accordance with the
-- Constitution of the Federation".
-- s 5(2): the Minister may by order in the Gazette (a) exempt any company or class of companies; (b) substitute the amount.
--
-- Local companies are measured by paid-up capital, foreign companies by authorised capital. Any other business vehicle (a sole
-- proprietorship, a partnership, a limited liability partnership) is outside s 5 altogether.
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a local company`
    `a foreign company`
    `another kind of business`

-- The printed figure. An order under s 5(2)(b) could change it; none was retrieved.
`the membership threshold` MEANS 500000

GIVEN `the entity` IS A Entity, `paid-up share capital` IS A NUMBER, `authorised share capital` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the capital test` IF
    CONSIDER `the entity`
    WHEN `a local company` THEN `paid-up share capital` AT LEAST `the membership threshold`
    WHEN `a foreign company` THEN `authorised share capital` AT LEAST `the membership threshold`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the entity` IS A Entity, `paid-up share capital` IS A NUMBER, `authorised share capital` IS A NUMBER,
      `exempted by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN, `membership terminated under the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member by force of the Act` IF
        `meets the capital test` `the entity` `paid-up share capital` `authorised share capital`
    AND (NOT `exempted by Ministerial order`)
    AND (NOT `membership terminated under the Constitution`)

§§ `12 -- subscriptions`

-- s 12(1): every company that is a member "by virtue of this Act" MUST pay an annual or periodic subscription "of such amount as may
-- be (a) determined by the Council after consultation with the Board; and (b) approved by the Minister".
-- (2): the Council may, with the same consultation and approval, divide members into classes, set different amounts, vary them, and
-- "determine the rate of interest" on subscriptions left unpaid.
-- (3): "The amount of subscription prescribed as being payable by any member ... must not exceed IN THE AGGREGATE $1,500 IN ANY
-- CALENDAR YEAR."
-- (4): it "may be recovered by the Council by an action for a debt in any court of competent jurisdiction". [33/2018]
--
-- The duty in s 12(1) binds only statutory members: a company that joined the Federation voluntarily is not within s 12. Whether the
-- interest set under s 12(2)(d) counts toward the $1,500 aggregate is not said; this encoding counts subscriptions only (an
-- inference from "amount of subscription").
`the annual subscription cap` MEANS 1500

GIVEN `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscription is within the cap` IF
    `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` AT MOST `the annual subscription cap`

GIVEN `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount above the cap` MEANS
    IF `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` GREATER THAN `the annual subscription cap`
    THEN `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` MINUS `the annual subscription cap`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can lawfully be charged` MEANS
    IF `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` GREATER THAN `the annual subscription cap`
    THEN `the annual subscription cap`
    ELSE `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year`

GIVEN `is a statutory member` IS A BOOLEAN, `amount set by the Council after consulting the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subscription is payable under s 12` IF
        `is a statutory member`
    AND `amount set by the Council after consulting the Board`
    AND `approved by the Minister`
    AND `the subscription is within the cap` `subscriptions prescribed in the calendar year`

§§ `9 -- the Board's information powers and the offences`

-- s 9(1): the Board or any authorised person is entitled "at all reasonable times, to full and free access" to the accounting and
-- other records. (2): either may require "any person" to disclose or furnish information or documents "which such person possesses or
-- has access to" as considered necessary (a) to ascertain whether the funds were applied in furtherance of the objects; or (b) for the
-- Board's functions.
-- (3): any person who (a) "without reasonable excuse, fails to comply" with a requirement under (2); (b) furnishes information or a
-- document "which the person knows or has reason to believe is false"; or (c) "hinders, obstructs or delays" the Board or an
-- authorised person, "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000".
--
-- No imprisonment is provided, and the burden of the reasonable excuse is not allocated by the text.
GIVEN `was required under s 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `furnished something known or believed false` IS A BOOLEAN, `hindered, obstructed or delayed the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits an offence under s 9(3)` IF
        (`was required under s 9(2)` AND (NOT `complied`) AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `furnished something known or believed false`
    OR  `hindered, obstructed or delayed the Board`

`the maximum fine under s 9(3)` MEANS 1000

§§ `4 and the Schedule -- the Council`

-- s 4(1): the Council "must include (a) one nominee from each of the local ethnic chambers of commerce and industry specified in the
-- Schedule; and (b) such number of representatives from foreign chambers of commerce and industry, NOT EXCEEDING ONE-QUARTER of the
-- total number of members of the Council". Schedule: 1. Singapore Chinese Chamber of Commerce and Industry; 2. Singapore Indian
-- Chamber of Commerce and Industry; 3. Singapore Malay Chamber of Commerce and Industry. (2): the Minister may amend the Schedule.
--
-- Read literally, "must include ... such number ... not exceeding one-quarter" sets only a ceiling; zero foreign representatives
-- satisfies it. The quarter is tested without rounding: foreign seats times 4 at most the Council size.
GIVEN `foreign chamber representatives` IS A NUMBER, `Council size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `foreign representation is within the quarter` IF
    `foreign chamber representatives` TIMES 4 AT MOST `Council size`

GIVEN `has a Chinese Chamber nominee` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an Indian Chamber nominee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has a Malay Chamber nominee` IS A BOOLEAN, `foreign chamber representatives` IS A NUMBER, `Council size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council is composed as s 4 requires` IF
        `has a Chinese Chamber nominee`
    AND `has an Indian Chamber nominee`
    AND `has a Malay Chamber nominee`
    AND `foreign representation is within the quarter` `foreign chamber representatives` `Council size`

§§ `7(2) -- what needs the Board's approval`

-- s 7(2): "The approval of the Board is required for the following matters: (a) the annual report and accounts ...; (b) the annual
-- budget ...; (c) the acquisition, sale, lease, mortgage, alienation or disposal ... of any movable or immovable property of such
-- value as the Board may determine; (d) the appointment of members of the Council; (e) any proposed amendment to or variation of the
-- Constitution". Item (c) is caught only at or above a value the Board sets; this encoding takes the value as a given.
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `the annual report and accounts`
    `the annual budget`
    `a property dealing at or above the Board's value`
    `a property dealing below the Board's value`
    `appointing a Council member`
    `amending the Constitution`
    `admitting a voluntary member`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs the Board's approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `a property dealing below the Board's value` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `admitting a voluntary member` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8(2), (3) -- the auditor`

-- s 8(2): the accounts "must be audited by an auditor appointed by the Council with the approval of the Board". (3): "A person is not
-- qualified for appointment as an auditor ... unless the person is a public accountant within the meaning of the Companies Act 1967."
GIVEN `appointed by the Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a public accountant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor is validly appointed` IF
    `appointed by the Council` AND `approved by the Board` AND `is a public accountant`

§§ `10 and 11 -- dissolution and the Constitution`

-- s 10(1): "The Federation must not be dissolved without the prior approval of the Minister." (2): on dissolution its property "must
-- be disposed of in such manner as may be determined by its members and approved by the Board".
-- s 11(1): any provision of the Constitution "that is inconsistent with this Act shall, to the extent of the inconsistency, be void".
-- (2): nothing in the Act excuses the Federation from any other written law.
GIVEN `the Minister approved beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Federation may be dissolved` IF `the Minister approved beforehand`

GIVEN `determined by the members` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the property disposal on dissolution is proper` IF
    `determined by the members` AND `approved by the Board`

GIVEN `inconsistent with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Constitution provision has effect` IF NOT `inconsistent with the Act`
